  "problem_understood": true,
  "business_impact": "Without a dedicated online portal, MapleSure's licensed group-benefits advisors must rely on phone and email to interact with service staff, who then re-key data into internal systems. This is inefficient and prone to errors. The creation of an Advisor Portal with a secure sign-in would streamline advisor interactions, enhance security, and lay the groundwork for future advisor-facing features.",
  "affected_applications": [
    "advisor-portal-signin"
  ],
  "stakeholders": [
    "Group Benefits Operations"
  ],
  "dependencies": [
    "Implementation of local credential store",
    "Development of sign-in page with email and password fields",
    "Flask-based routing setup for sign-in and welcome pages"
  ],
  "risks": [
    "The application is in the early development phase, meaning any delays in setting up the initial framework could impact future feature delivery."
  ],
  "clarification_questions": [
    "What are the details and specifications for the demonstration advisor accounts that need to be seeded into the local credential store?"
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "This initial release will not require integration with any external identity providers.",
    "There will be no need for advanced security features like multi-factor authentication in the first release."
  ],
  "business_rules": [
    {
      "rule_id": "BR-1",
      "text": "The application must present a sign-in page with an email address field and a password field, reachable at the application root."
    },
    {
      "rule_id": "BR-2",
      "text": "The sign-in form must validate input before submission: both fields are required, and the email address must be well-formed. Validation messages must appear next to the field they concern."
    },
    {
      "rule_id": "BR-3",
      "text": "The password field must be masked by default and must provide a show/hide toggle."
    },
    {
      "rule_id": "BR-4",
      "text": "Submitted credentials must be checked against a local credential store seeded with demonstration advisor accounts; no external identity provider is called in this release."
    },
    {
      "rule_id": "BR-5",
      "text": "A failed sign-in must show a single generic error message that does not reveal whether the email address or the password was incorrect."
    },
    {
      "rule_id": "BR-6",
      "text": "A successful sign-in must land the advisor on a welcome page that greets them by name and shows a visible sign-out control."
    },
    {
      "rule_id": "BR-7",
      "text": "Signing out must clear the session and return the advisor to the sign-in page; the welcome page must not be reachable after sign-out."
    }
  ],
